{"id":72,"date":"2011-07-24T08:00:29","date_gmt":"2011-07-24T13:00:29","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/?p=72"},"modified":"2011-07-24T08:00:29","modified_gmt":"2011-07-24T13:00:29","slug":"new-trip","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/2011\/07\/24\/new-trip\/","title":{"rendered":"New TRIP !!!"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>I been waiting for a while this new and long trip!<br \/>\nIn the same time, as I said in my last post, rather old now btw, time flies!<br \/>\nSo I&#8217;ve had great time back in Grenoble in our wonderfull association the &#8220;Pt&#8217;tit velo dans la tete&#8221; but its now over, and my great bike trip is on!<br \/>\nSo Ana and me started from Grenoble the 2 of July, direction Switzerland. we already knew a bit about this country, but this time we got a lot more that what we bargained for \ud83d\ude42  We wern&#8217;t expecting anything special, but a lot of happy and friendly things happened to us; Swiss people were very open and friendly people. From there Ana went to Basel to meet with a good friend of her for a 2 weeks females only bike trip. In the meantime, I&#8217;ve been on my own, riding mostly alone, going to visit other bile workshops in Bern, where I stayed for a few days. Then I decided not to go straight  to Germany as I was first planning to, but I wanted to stay a bit more in this great country, so I travelled toward Interlaken, and Luzern. In Luzern I stayed one night at an old host\/friend: Serge, a pragliding addict, very funny and friendly. This place were also the meet point with Alex, an other old friend (met first in Scotland), so I went with him to his parent&#8217;s place in Konstanz, Germany, next to a huge lake. Thereafter I travelled across Bavaria, under rather wet conditions, but people there made it anyway a great time. Cycling there is easy, safe and very enjoyable !<br \/>\nSo far, this trip is going in such a way, that I can only tell postive things about it; everything is really pleasant!<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>I been waiting for a while this new and long trip! In the same time, as I said in my last post, rather old now btw, time flies! So I&#8217;ve had great time back in Grenoble in our wonderfull association the &#8220;Pt&#8217;tit velo dans la tete&#8221; but its now over, and my great bike trip [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":177,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-72","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-uncategorized"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/72","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/177"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=72"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/72\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":73,"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/72\/revisions\/73"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=72"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=72"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/francoisbob.biketravellers.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=72"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}